// McMaster, Hamilton (you met at University)
// Context: You remember that you stayed out on your date under that tree and never mentioned to Clea that you had class in the observatory. You were looking forward to watching the meteor shower just wanted to keep spending time with her.
    // That was a pretty amazing date, wasn't it? [take a picture of the tree]
    // I wonder what the shower would have looked like from the observatory. [Take a picture of the observatory]
    // Now that I think about it, Clea used to make fun of those people taking engagement photos under that arch! [take a photo of the arch]
    // That's new! I wonder if we would have had less arguments about where to eat with that option around [take a photo of the hotdog stand]
    // wow that sculpture is pretty weird, was that always there? [take a pic of the sculpture]

// Pioneer Village
// Context: You didn't realize it, but this place is closed down now, though you two worked here for a while when Clea was in medical school. It's downright spooky
    // Good thing Clea switched to guitar. The fiddle was not her instrument [take a picture of the band stand with a broken fiddle]
    // Yikes, I forgot about that time we got poison ivy. Not worth the minimum wage. [take a picture of the foliage]
    // Now people churn butter by sticking a bag of heavy cream in a fanny pack and running around... the future is truly here! [take a picture of the old-timey butter churn]
    // There's really no one I would rather wear an itchy pioneer dress with in the August sun [take a picture of the fallen clothes line with pioneer dresses on it]
    // It's cool that the sun and stars have been playing such an important role in human lives for so long [take a picture of the sundial]

// The Peach Palace (knock-off Apple Factory)
//Context: The first time you went to Clea's family's cottage, you had really wanted to bring something nice, so you stopped to get a pie. You had been getting late, and you two just couldn't agree on what pie to get. When you finally settled on the last peach cobbler, you were so frustrated that you didn't notice the crack in the pavement. You went tumbling and so did the pie. 
    // Damn, he creepy [take a picture of the apple man]
    // She's so beautiful. I can't help but feel like that's what Clea will look like in 50 years [Ask the woman if you can take her picture]
    // I think that argument was the only time I made Clea cry in public. I don't think I regret anything more than that. [take a picture of the pie stand]
    // A nice ceramic would obviously have been the better choice [take a picture of the peach-shaped serving dish in the window (or a mug, or a vase, or whatever)]
    // I always liked how clear the night skies could be this far from the city [take a picture of the setting sun]
title: Setup
---
// Track sentiments for dialogue
<<declare $contempt= 0>>
<<declare $fondness= 0>>
<<declare $codependence= 0>>
<<declare $astronomy = 0>>
<<declare $avoidant= 0>>

// Which photos were taken where
<<declare $photo_MacDougal = 0>> // 1 through 5
<<declare $photo_City = 0>>
<<declare $photo_Town = 0>>
<<declare $photo_Peach = 0>>

//Car Scene Index
<<declare $car_scene_number = 0>>
===


title: Start
---
<<if $car_scene_number == 0>>
    <<jump Car_Scene_0>>
<<elseif $car_scene_number == 1>>
    <<jump Car_Scene_1>>
<<endif>>
===
title: Car_Scene_0
---
// BLACK SCREEN

// JOSH - Maybe some folly of moving a bag into a car?
Clea: Is that everything?
You: Yeah

You start the car.
// JOSH - associated sounds

You: Wait!

You shuffle through your bag, and sigh in relief when you find it.
// JOSH - associated sounds

You: Just wanted to make sure I had my camera
<<FadeIn>>
// JOSH - You hear the car take off. Lo-Fi music starts
// TITLE CARD: "3.5 HOURS TO THE COTTAGE"
Clea: ...
You: ...
Clea: Hey, I wanted to apologize for- 
You: It's okay. I'm just glad we could make this trip happen.
Clea: Me too. I know it's important to you. 
You: Yeah. After this, it might get harder to visit your parents' cottage for a while, you know?
Clea: (Laughs) We're moving to Vancouver, not Antarctica.
You: No, I know! But that's still across the country, and you'll be busy with your internship.
You: I'm just saying, you might- We might not be able to fly home every year.
Clea: Yeah you're probably right...
Clea: Vancouver should be pretty fun though.
You: Bah! Only if you like FRESH AIR and MOUNTAINS and... PROVIDING HEALTHCARE!
Clea: Which we... hate?
You: Absolutely. We crave Toronto smog. And pestilence.

//FADE TO BLACK
//FADE IN
<<FadeOut>>
You pass a road sign that says 10 km to MacDougal University
<<FadeIn>>
You: Oh shit, I didn't realize we'd be so close to MacDougal
Clea: Ooh, how romantic.
Clea: I'm joking, obviously. Kinda. People literally take engagement photos there.
You: That's true, people love taking photos under that one arch.
Clea: It's a romantic arch.
You: I mean it's a teeny bit traumatic. University, not the arch. At least it was for those of us who weren't amazing at school.
You: Traumatic... but also romantic.
You think about it for a second.
You: Actually, do you wanna walk around campus for a bit?
Clea: You know what, why not? We've got time.
You: Nice! I really sold you with "traumatic but romantic," didn't I?
Clea: And I have to pee.
You: Oh sure.

// FADE TO BLACK
<<FadeOut>>

<<declare $MacDougal_tree_5_read= false>>
<<declare $observatory_after_tree = false>>
<<set $car_scene_number += 1>>


You stop in at MacDougal University. If you're honest with yourself, it is kind of romantic. It's where you two met, after all.
// ADD SCENE TRANSITION COMMAND - MACDOUGAL
<<SetLocation 0>>
<<Transition 2>>
===

title: TakePicture
---
<<TakePicture Player>>
Is this the memory you want to keep? You can only keep one Polaroid from this location.
-> Yes
    <<Keep Polaroid>>
-> No
    <<Discard Polaroid>>
