    You: Now that's how you ride a horse. What a legend.
    Clea: I think some engineers tried to get up there to take a grad photo on the horse once
    You: Wait, you're telling me that statue isn't new?
    Clea: What, Dougal MacDougal? Of course he isn't new.
    You: You're making that up
    Clea: Are you sure you actually went here?
-> Take Photo
    <<jump TakePicture>>
-> Leave
===
title: MacDougal_observatory_4
---
-> Remember that time you skipped class at the observatory
    <<if $MacDougal_tree_5_read == false>>
        You're staring at the observatory when Clea points out the tree from your first date
        -> Reminisce about the tree from your first date
            <<set $observatory_after_tree = true>>
            <<LookAt Player MacDougal_tree_5>>
            <<jump MacDougal_tree_5>>
        -> Keep looking at the observatory
            <<set $contempt+=1>>
            You remember the meteor shower you were supposed to watch from the observatory.
            You imagine in must have been more beautiful from up there than under the tree, where you watched it with Clea that night. Not that you told her that, obviously.
    <<else>>
        <<jump MacDougal_observatory_4_alt>> 
    <<endif>>
-> Take Photo
    <<jump TakePicture>>
    -> Leave
===
title: MacDougal_tree_5
---
-> Reminisce about the tree from your first date
    <<set $MacDougal_tree_5_read = true>>
    You: Shall we sit under that tree again?
    Clea: God, we talked under there for so long.
    You: Don't forget, we did start at the ice cream shop. I didn't intentionally take you on a date to a tree.
    Clea: No but it was my favourite part.
    You: Yeah. Talking to you was like... the easiest thing I have ever done in my life
    Clea: Exactly. We probably could have talked all night. Why didn't we?
    You: Bugs.
    Clea nods sagely
    Clea: Bugs.
    You: But I'm glad we stayed out long enough to catch the meteor shower.
    Clea: Oh my god, I can't believe I forgot about that! It was beautiful.
    It WAS beautiful. Clea was beautiful too.
    <<if $observatory_after_tree== true>>
        -> return to looking at the observatory
            <<LookAt Player MacDougal_observatory_4>>
            <<jump MacDougal_observatory_4_alt>>
    <<endif>>
-> Take Photo
    <<jump TakePicture>>
-> Leave
===
title: MacDougal_observatory_4_alt
---
You never told Clea that you were supposed to watch the meteor shower from the observatory the night of your first date.
It hadn't seemed to matter. In that moment, you felt like you belonged under that tree with her.
In this moment, you realize how much it still matters to you that you missed out on the observatory.
