===
title: Breakup
---
Clea: Is that everything?
You: ...
Clea: Jessie?
<<if $avoidant< 1>>
    You can see that she knows what's coming, but it doesn't make this any easier.
<<elseif $avoidant > 2>>
    If there's any part of you that doesn't want to move to Vancouver, any instinct telling you that this relationship is over, it's very quiet.
    In fact, everything's pretty much great, isn't it?
    If it isn't, you really can't recall.
    You've just been on a goofy little road trip and everything is great!
    Wahoo!
    Some things aren't worth thinking about, you know?
    <<jump Cottage_End>>
<<else>>
    Part of you really doesn't want to talk about this. But you push forward.
<<endif>>
-> Tell her you love her
<< if $fondness > 1>>
    You: I love you so much, Clea.
    Tears start to well in Clea's eyes. In yours too. You're not really sure which one of you started crying first, actually.
    Clea: I love you too.
<<else>>
You can't seem to get the words out.
You know you loved her once.
But it feels like a distant memory now.
<<endif>>
-> Try to end things
<<if $contempt > 2>>
    You: It's over for us.
    Clea: Wait, what? Are you fucking serious?
    Clea: You break up with me MOMENTS before we get to the cottage YOU insisted on going to, and all you have to say for yourself is "It's over for us?"
    Clea: You're being an asshole right now.
    You kind of feel like it's Clea who's being an asshole, or at least being unfair to you.
    It's not like she's perfect.
    <<if $photo_MacDougal==2>>
        She was kind of a snob about people taking engagement photos under the MacDougall arch, even if she likes to pretend that she's always found it romantic.
    <<endif>>
    <<if $photo_Town==2>>
        She's really not as good of a musician as she likes to think. Clea playing the fiddle? Awful.
    <<endif>>
    <<if $photo_Peach==2>>
        You don't even want to think about how bad she is at gift-giving. Who would try to get the peach cobbler that's been sitting out all day when there are perfectly good ceramics to buy?
    <<endif>>
<<elseif $codependence >1>>
    You: Despite our best efforts, we aren't always good for each other.
    <<if $photo_MacDougal == 1>>
        You think about the hotdog cart, and how you and Clea were so attached yet so conflict-prone at MacDougal.
        You: We fight about the silliest stuff, like where to eat. Yet we can't seem to handle time apart.
    <<endif>>
    <<if $photo_Town == 4>>
        You remember the stupid poison ivy debacle. You know it wasn't the only time you made things worse for each other.
        Sometimes, you love someone so much that it makes you do stupid things.
        You: We can't help but get stuck in each other's messes.
    <<endif>>
    <<if $photo_Peach ==4>>
        You can't get the fight at the Peach Palace out of your head.
        You: I hate that I made you cry at the Peach Palace of all places. I can be so mean to you sometimes.
        Clea: (Shaking her head) I'm not trying to absolve you, but I don't think it's normal to cry over a simple disagreement like that.
        Clea: I couldn't handle the fact that you disagreed with me. I don't know...
        Clea: I think I care too much about what you think, sometimes. Maybe if I cared a little less, I wouldn't have cried.
        You: I don't know that that's fair.
    <<endif>>
    You: And I have to believe that it's possible to love someone without getting too enmeshed. But I don't think we've ever figured that out.
<<elseif $fondness >1>>
    You: It's not that I don't love you. We have so many wonderful memories.
    <<if $photo_MacDougal == 5>>
    You remember your incredible first date.
    You: I could talk to you forever.
    <<endif>>
    <<if $photo_Town == 3>>
    You remember trying to make Clea smile with your performances at Old Timey Town
    You: I've always loved making you laugh
    <<endif>>
    <<if $photo_Peach == 1>>
    You think about Clea growing old without you, and you can't breathe.
    You want that woman to be so happy.
    You just don't think you can be the person who makes her happy anymore.
    <<endif>>
    You: I don't think I realized that I could love you this much and let you go.
    You: I want so much for you, and I just don't think I can be a part of it.
    Clea: I want the world for you too. I love you so so much.
<<endif>>
Clea: So this is it? We're really breaking up?
You: I'm sorry.
Clea: I'm sorry too.
You: ...
Clea: ...
Clea: So the cottage...
You: Probably not such a great idea for me to come anymore, right?
<<if $contempt>2 >>
    Clea: No, I don't think it is.
<<else>>
    Clea: I mean you're still welcome, if it's what you want.
<<endif>>
<<if $astronomy >1>>
    <<if $photo_MacDougal == 4>>
        You think about the observatory again. You think about the meteor shower happening tonight
    <<endif>>
    <<if $photo_Town == 1>>
        You think about the sun dial, and you realize that you've never stopped thinking about the stars.
    <<endif>>
    <<if $photo_Peach == 3>>
        You think about how clear the sky can be out here. What better night to be here than during a meteor shower.
    <<endif>>
    You: I was thinking I might take the car and find a place to watch the meteor shower. If you're ok with that.
    Clea: Yeah, you can have the car.
<<else>>
    You: I don't know. I think I'll have to figure something else out.
<<endif>>
<<SetLocation 3>>
<<Transition 2>>
===